WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.420
[intro music]

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:14.840
Good morning, Hank, it's Thursday!

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:20.260
Hank, after a long delay because of snow in Columbus, Ohio, I've finally reached Houston, Texas, where

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.140
by the grace of God,

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:24.480
it is not snowing.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:28.820
There was one really cool thing about the Columbus airport, though: they had Nerd Fighters!

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:30.400
Nerd Fighters!

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:36.680
Here's my question about Nerd Fighters: Is Nerd Fighters a game about people who fight against nerds?

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:40.260
Or is it a game about nerds who fight against other people?

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:44.220
I've come to believe that Nerd Fighters is a game about nerds who fight.

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:47.020
Nerds who tackle the scourge of popular people.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:51.160
And I've been thinking to myself, "this would be a great video game."

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:54.620
It could be like a mix between Mortal Kombat and Mike Tyson's Punch-out!

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:59.560
Like, first you pick your character. Everyone would totally have their own special powers.

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:03.940
Like, the band geek would be, like, "I will destroy your ears with my tuba!"

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:07.860
And the theater guy would be like, "I am an expert at sword-fighting!"

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:09.900
And the English nerd would be like...

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:11.240
um...

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:13.160
"I know a lot of Shakespeare quotes!"

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:18.600
Using the English nerd when you're playing Nerd Fighters is kind of like using Toad when you're playing Super Mario Kart.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:22.220
So you would pick your Nerd Fighter, and then you would go to war with popular people.

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:26.260
The Mike Tyson of the game would be the quarterback of the high school football team.

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:30.680
And you'd have to dodge his uppercuts and dodge his uppercuts and dodge his uppercuts and then jab!

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:34.740
I mean, to be honest, I've never even really understood the war between nerds and popular people.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.980
Like, who do-who do-who do you guys got?

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:40.780
Uh, we got like, George W. Bush, and, like, Tom Brady.

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:48.420
OK, well, I see your George W. Bush with Bill Clinton, and I raise you Abraham Lincoln and Franklin Delano Roosevelt.

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:49.320
And

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:57.340
I can easily see your Tom Brady with the thinking man's football player Tiki Barber, and I think I can raise you, hm

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:01.260
An Isaac Newton, a William Shakespeare, a Blaise Pascal, an Albert Einstein, an Immanuel Kant,

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:05.780
an Aristotle, a Jane Austen, a Bill Gates, a Mahatma Gandhi, a Nelson Mandela, and all four Beatles.

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:07.320
We win!

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.800
And yet, Hank, the war continues.

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:12.300
You know what we need for Nerd Fighters?

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:13.980
We need a theme song.

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:21.420
[singing] "We've got calculators and trombones!
We've got D&amp;D and Star Wars drones!"

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:26.000
They're in their original box, too, which makes them a lot more valuable.

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:32.420
[singing] "Nerd Fighters, we're fighting nerds,
We're no longer just using our words!"

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.860
Although, by and large, we are really articulate.

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:36.680
So

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:43.840
[singing] When I'm not watchin' Battlestar Galactica
I'm designing weapons that'll kick your ass-tica!

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:50.260
Nerd Fighters, we fight with our brains,
Nerd Fighters, we bring the frakkin' pain!

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:56.520
It's a reference to a sci-fi show, I don't know. I mean, maybe you never saw those really.

00:02:56.520 --> 00:03:05.480
It was a really good show, um, I liked it a lot, and, um, some of my friends liked it, I mean not, they're not real friends, I just know them on the internet.

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:08.860
Hank, now that you've successfully completed the Strawberry Hill Challenge,

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:13.560
I feel like it's time that we had some more challenges, so maybe you or our viewers can start suggesting some.

